            "contribution_type": "sourcing",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Decide where you want to install the fan. Most fans are placed in the center of the room, allowing smooth air flow throughout the room. However, larger rooms may be better suited for 2 fans for optimal air flow. For safety reasons, do not install a fan over a bed.<ref>https://www.homedepot.com/c/ab/best-ceiling-fans/9ba683603be9fa5395fab90b9b26067</ref> [[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 1.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Consider various room factors:<ref>https://www.houzz.com/magazine/how-to-choose-a-ceiling-fan-for-comfort-and-style-stsetivw-vs~98090656</ref> [[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Think about electricity. Since fans require the same amount of power as most ceiling fixtures, the electrical circuit shouldn’t be overloaded.<ref>https://www.thisoldhouse.com/ideas/how-to-size-ceiling-fan</ref> [[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "# Choose a good quality fan. A cheap fan is more trouble than it is worth. Not only will a cheap fan wobble, but a poor-quality fan will not circulate as much air at a given RPM.<ref>https://www.houzz.com/magazine/how-to-choose-a-ceiling-fan-for-comfort-and-style-stsetivw-vs~98090656</ref> [[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "",
                    "==References==",
                    "{{reflist}}"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Decide where you want to install the fan. Most fans are placed in the center of the room, allowing smooth air flow throughout the room. However, larger rooms may be better suited for 2 fans for optimal air flow. For safety reasons, do not install a fan over a bed.[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 1.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Consider various room factors:[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Think about electricity. Since fans require the same amount of power as most ceiling fixtures, the electrical circuit shouldn’t be overloaded.[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "# Choose a good quality fan. A cheap fan is more trouble than it is worth. Not only will a cheap fan wobble, but a poor-quality fan will not circulate as much air at a given RPM.[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 4.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
