        {
            "id": "18349817",
            "user": "Hootooshay",
            "timestamp": "07:04, 1 September 2015",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(6,076 bytes)",
            "change": 904,
            "summary": "(RCP reverted edits by Superfanseo (talk) to  revision #18343409 by Votebot)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "",
                    "#Decide where you want to install the fan. Most fans are placed in the center of the room, allowing smooth air flow throughout the room. However, larger rooms may be better suited for 2 fans for optimal air flow. For safety reasons, do not install a fan over a bed.[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 1.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Consider various room factors:[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Room Size",
                    "#**30\" ceiling fan for rooms up to 8' x 10' (small bedrooms, walk-in closets, smaller kitchens)",
                    "#**42\" ceiling fan for rooms up to 12' x 12' (medium bedrooms, kitchens, small recreation areas)",
                    "#**52\" ceiling fan for rooms up to 18' x 20' (large bedrooms, family rooms, great rooms, dining rooms)",
                    "#*Ceiling Height",
                    "#**Low ceiling: Hugger mount or traditional- mount without down rod",
                    "#**Standard 8' ceiling: traditional- mount with down rod",
                    "#**9' or Higher ceiling: Extended down rod",
                    "#**Sloped ceiling: Extended down rod",
                    "#*You will need to check the floor to ceiling height of the blades. Make sure you take into account the distance that the fan hangs from the ceiling.",
                    "#**For safety, a minimum height of 7’-9’ is recommended. If your fan does not meet the 7’ recommendation, you can look into a low-ceiling mount. Building codes in your area may require this.",
                    "#**For optimum air circulation it is most efficient to have the fan blade 8' to 9' above the floor. For higher ceilings see the chart for recommended down rod length.",
                    "#Think about electricity. Since fans require the same amount of power as most ceiling fixtures, the electrical circuit shouldn’t be overloaded.[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*If the fan includes a light fixture, ensure that the circuit is able to handle both the fan and light. If your circuit will not hold this capacity then a new circuit must be run from the home’s main panel to the fan.",
                    "#*If there was not a preexisting fixture, you will need to create a place to hang the fan. If your home is not wired properly, some fans do have swag wiring that can be plugged into a wall outlet, but ceiling installation is preferred.",
                    "#*It is easiest to install ceiling bracing and electrical wiring during new home construction even if you will be installing a fan at a later time.",
                    "#*Consulting an electrician is always your best option.",
                    "# Choose a good quality fan. A cheap fan is more trouble than it is worth. Not only will a cheap fan wobble, but a poor-quality fan will not circulate as much air at a given RPM.[[Image:Choose the Right Ceiling Fan Step 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*While speed helps control how much air is moved, blade pitch (angle between blade and horizontal) and design also play a role. Good quality fans boast motors that have more power, so as to allow for greater blade pitch. Cheap fans, on the other hand, have motors that are not strong enough to handle the air resistance associated with greater blade pitch, requiring the manufacturer to lower the blade pitch to avoid burning out the motor.",
                    "#*Also, cheap fans produce a humming noise. Remember that a good-quality fan will not always be priced unreasonably high. Even Hunter ceiling fans, which can be found at stores such as Lowes or Home Depot, are of decent quality for reasonable price.",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#[[Image:A1 c1.jpg|right]]Superfan has brought innovation to a highly common domestic product that is used by millions of households by saving valuable energy, adding more comforts and eliminating many pain-points for consumers.",
                    "#Superfan is a ceiling fan that consumes less than half the electricity compared to the normal ceiling fans while delivering the same amount of air. Superfan achieves its low consumption by using a super-efficient BLDC motor and microprocessor controlled digital inverter. Superfan does not use troublesome regulators and comes with a sleek and not easily breakable remote to control its speed.  The speeds are precise and stable even when the supply voltage varies, even at as low as 140V or as high as 300V.Superfan has been designed and is manufactured in India by Versa Drives Private Limited, Coimbatore.",
                    "#Superfan has other highly useful features like high air delivery, remote operation, no troublesome regulator, top speed in even in low voltage, no speed change due to supply variation and rugged construction for long life. More details can be had from www.superfan.in. Superfan is also green product with ROHS electronics, plastic bag & thermocole free recyclable packing & VOC free painting.",
                    "#The Managing Director of the Versa Drives,   Mr. Sundar Muruganandhan says “Our experience of 24 years in industrial products has helped in making a robust design for reliable and long lasting ceiling fan. With this we want to create awareness in customer’s mind to think more about ceiling fans than normally they do. Major users like hospitals, educational institutes and commercial offices can enjoy savings of more than 1000 rupees per fan every year as ROI by using Superfan”.  The company aims at catering to all looking for energy saving as ceiling fans consume a considerable power in every home and its additional features like remote control, low & wide voltage operation and running twice longer & quietly with inverter should prompt more buyers.",
                    "#There are three models and six exciting colours in each model are available to attract the customers. Currently customers can order Superfan by phone or email or online through website www.superfan.in and www.ceilingfanindia.com to receive the products at their doorsteps or from local dealers. Superfan comes with a 5-year warranty on its motor."
                ]
            }
        },
